<p>U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio ended a two-day visit to Rome on Friday after meeting Pope Leo XIV, Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni and Foreign Minister Antonio Tajani for talks on U.S. relations with the Vatican and Italy, the war involving the United States, Israel and Iran, NATO and migration. The trip followed President Trump’s public criticism of Pope Leo over the pontiff’s opposition to the Iran war and criticism of Italy and other European allies over what the U.S. administration describes as insufficient support for efforts to confront Iran and reopen the Strait of Hormuz. Rubio urged European governments to move beyond statements and act against Iran, saying he did not understand why allies would not support U.S. efforts and warning that Tehran’s claim to control access to an international waterway could set a wider precedent. The Vatican said its talks with Rubio included the “need to work tirelessly in favour of peace” and a renewed commitment to good bilateral relations, while Meloni described her meeting as a frank exchange between allies who defend their national interests and recognize the value of Western unity. Rubio also said he remained a strong supporter of NATO but that President Trump would decide whether to withdraw U.S. troops from European bases if allies refused to allow their use in what Washington considers serious emergencies.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/M-G2F8Gsf3bQOXoOJN4CbI9QwIwwolDU9UohIZuU_FNSsvgPGRY_cYtUXPYAMfYhUe4nlyC2erGoFvkuZk_wFKWy8bl2klI9aePCuNUrqg' alt='Italy&#x27;s Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni welcomes U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio at Palazzo Chigi in Rome on May 8, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Vatican timing: Dawn reported the papal encounter lasted 45 minutes; Business Recorder said Rubio spent 2-1/2 hours at the Vatican before leaving in a convoy under tight security.</li><li>Troop-threat context: Aaj News said Trump had already announced the withdrawal of 5,000 troops from Germany and threatened pullouts from Italy and Spain over their refusal to get involved in the conflict.</li><li>Lebanon file: La Voz de Galicia reported that Rubio said Italy could do a lot for Lebanon, one regional issue raised around the Rome talks.</li><li>Meeting length: Rubio and Meloni met for about 90 minutes at Palazzo Chigi after Rubio held talks with Tajani at the Farnesina.</li></ul><blockquote>The fundamental question every country, not just Italy, needs to ask themselves is, are you going to normalise a country claiming to control an international waterway? - Marco Rubio</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Vatican: The Vatican said Rubio’s meetings included an exchange of views on the world situation, the need to work for peace and a renewed commitment to good bilateral relations. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/07/marco-rubio-to-meet-pope-at-the-vatican-after-trump-attacks-on-pontiff'>The Guardian</a>, <a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1998666/vaticans-careful-words-on-pope-rubio-meeting-imply-deep-tensions-with-trump-say-analysts'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Giorgia Meloni: Meloni said the talks covered bilateral relations, the Middle East, security, freedom of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz, Libya, Lebanon, Ukraine and China, and called the meeting constructive and frank. (<a href='https://roma.corriere.it/politica/diretta-live/26_maggio_08/rubio-incontra-meloni-e-tajani-a-roma-la-diretta-live-alla-farnesina-per-parlare-dei-rapporti-italia-usa.shtml'>Corriere della Sera</a>)</li><li>Marco Rubio: Rubio described the talks with Meloni as an excellent meeting and called the U.S.-Italy relationship a strategic partnership. (<a href='https://roma.corriere.it/politica/diretta-live/26_maggio_08/rubio-incontra-meloni-e-tajani-a-roma-la-diretta-live-alla-farnesina-per-parlare-dei-rapporti-italia-usa.shtml'>Corriere della Sera</a>)</li><li>Peter Martin: Former U.S. diplomat Peter Martin said the Vatican’s statement showed there was work to 